IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ccc-core`
IMPORT `ccc30-forms-actors`

-- ccc30-forms-preservation.l4 -- FORM 5.001 to FORM 5.0091 of the Criminal Code (Canada), R.S.C., 1985, c. C-46 (raw text lines 17499-17719):
-- the preservation demand and order, the keep-account-open order, the production orders, the information to revoke or vary, and the non-disclosure order.
-- Source: a plain-text rendering, made by a converter script, of the Justice Laws Website consolidation (current to 2026-09-30); it is not the
-- official text and nothing here is claimed verified against the official text.
-- WHAT IS A RULE HERE. The informations (5.002, 5.0031, 5.004, 5.0081, 5.009) are the officer's application: their "the informant says" recitals are
-- prescribed wording, and the grounds they recite are the grounds of sections 487.012 to 487.0191, which another part owns. What each Form says to the
-- PERSON it is addressed to is encoded: how long a duty lasts and what ends it, the time to produce, what contravening it can cost, the right to
-- apply to revoke or vary, and the periods the informations ask for.
-- WHO IS BOUND. The core's `Party` has no constructor for "(name of person)", the financial institution, person or entity a demand or order is addressed to,
-- so `forms 1 to 23 addressee` is declared here (NEEDS-CORE.md asks for the constructor).
-- How a result reads: JUST TRUE; JUST FALSE (the text says no in its own words); NOTHING (not covered). Every JUST FALSE branch carries a FALSE-kind
-- comment that quotes the words; every NOTHING branch carries a NOTHING-kind comment. A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE.
-- "may be subject to a fine" states a liability, and no amount: how much is outside the text (NOTHING-kind: points outside the text), so nothing here computes a fine.

§ `Forms 5.001 to 5.0091 -- who is bound and what a contravention can cost`

DECLARE `forms 5.001 to 5.0091 action` IS ONE OF
    `form 5.005 produces the document to the peace officer or public officer`
    `form 5.0091 discloses the existence of the demand or order`

-- What the Forms say a contravention may cost: "a fine", "imprisonment", or "both" (the Forms print "a fine, to imprisonment or to both").
DECLARE `forms 5.001 to 5.0091 consequence` IS ONE OF
    `forms 5.001 to 5.0091 a fine`
    `forms 5.001 to 5.0091 imprisonment`
    `forms 5.001 to 5.0091 both a fine and imprisonment`

§ `Form 5.001 -- Preservation demand (subsection 487.012(1))`

-- "you are required to preserve (specify the computer data) that is in your possession or control when you receive this demand until (insert date) unless,
-- before that date, this demand is revoked or a document that contains that data is obtained under a warrant or an order."
-- Each limb that fails answers JUST FALSE: "when" counts as "where"; "until" is a bar (JUST TRUE before the date, JUST FALSE after it);
-- "unless" once met ends the duty. The date is read as the last day of the duty (a fork: NOTES.md F-A).
-- src:17508 | you are required to preserve (specify the computer data) that is in your possession or control when you receive this demand until (insert date) unless, before that date, this demand is revoked or a document that contains that data is obtained under a warrant or an order.
@ref Form 5.001 (Subsection 487.012(1)) Preservation Demand, the duty to preserve (src:17508)
GIVEN `the computer data was in the person's possession or control when the person received the demand` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day in question` IS A DATE
      `the date inserted in the demand` IS A DATE
      `the demand was revoked before that date` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a document that contains the data was obtained under a warrant or an order before that date` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`form 5.001 the person is required to preserve the computer data` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the computer data was in the person's possession or control when the person received the demand`
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "that is in your possession or control when you receive this demand"
        IF `the day in question` GREATER THAN `the date inserted in the demand`
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "until (insert date)"
        IF `the demand was revoked before that date`
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless, before that date, this demand is revoked"
        IF `a document that contains the data was obtained under a warrant or an order before that date`
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a document that contains that data is obtained under a warrant or an order"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- "If you contravene this demand without lawful excuse, you may be subject to a fine."
-- Not contravened: the "If" is unmet (JUST FALSE). Contravened but with a lawful excuse: the words "without lawful excuse" limit the sentence and the case falls outside
-- the limit (NOTHING). The demand names a fine only: imprisonment is not stated here (NOTHING).
-- src:17510 | If you contravene this demand without lawful excuse, you may be subject to a fine.
@ref Form 5.001 (Subsection 487.012(1)) Preservation Demand, contravention (src:17510)
GIVEN `the person contravened the demand` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has a lawful excuse` IS A BOOLEAN
      consequence IS A `forms 5.001 to 5.0091 consequence`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`form 5.001 contravening the demand without lawful excuse, the person may be subject to` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the person contravened the demand`
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If you contravene this demand without lawful excuse"
        IF `the person has a lawful excuse`
        THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "without lawful excuse"
        OTHERWISE
            CONSIDER consequence
            WHEN `forms 5.001 to 5.0091 a fine` THEN JUST TRUE
            WHEN `forms 5.001 to 5.0091 imprisonment` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the sentence names "a fine" only
            WHEN `forms 5.001 to 5.0091 both a fine and imprisonment` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the sentence names "a fine" only

-- "You are required to destroy the computer data that would not be retained in the ordinary course of business, and any document that is prepared for the purpose
-- of preserving the computer data, in accordance with section 487.0194 of the Criminal Code." When and how is in section 487.0194, outside the sources.
DECLARE `forms 5.001 and 5.003 thing to destroy` IS ONE OF
    `forms 5.001 and 5.003 computer data that would not be retained in the ordinary course of business`
    `forms 5.001 and 5.003 a document that is prepared for the purpose of preserving the computer data`
    `forms 5.001 and 5.003 something else`

-- src:17511 | You are required to destroy the computer data that would not be retained in the ordinary course of business, and any document that is prepared for the purpose of preserving the computer data, in accordance with section 487.0194 of the Criminal Code. If you contravene that provision without lawful excuse, you may be subject to a fine, to imprisonment or to both.
@ref Form 5.001 (Subsection 487.012(1)) Preservation Demand, the duty to destroy (src:17511)
GIVEN thing IS A `forms 5.001 and 5.003 thing to destroy`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`form 5.001 the person is required to destroy` MEANS
    CONSIDER thing
    WHEN `forms 5.001 and 5.003 computer data that would not be retained in the ordinary course of business` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `forms 5.001 and 5.003 a document that is prepared for the purpose of preserving the computer data` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `forms 5.001 and 5.003 something else` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the computer data that would not be retained in the ordinary course of business, and any document that is prepared for the purpose of preserving the computer data"

-- "If you contravene that provision without lawful excuse, you may be subject to a fine, to imprisonment or to both." (that provision: section 487.0194)
-- src:17511 | You are required to destroy the computer data that would not be retained in the ordinary course of business, and any document that is prepared for the purpose of preserving the computer data, in accordance with section 487.0194 of the Criminal Code. If you contravene that provision without lawful excuse, you may be subject to a fine, to imprisonment or to both.
@ref Form 5.001 (Subsection 487.012(1)) Preservation Demand, contravening section 487.0194 (src:17511)
GIVEN `the person contravened section 487.0194` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has a lawful excuse` IS A BOOLEAN
      consequence IS A `forms 5.001 to 5.0091 consequence`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`form 5.001 contravening section 487.0194 without lawful excuse, the person may be subject to` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the person contravened section 487.0194`
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If you contravene that provision without lawful excuse"
        IF `the person has a lawful excuse`
        THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "without lawful excuse"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE   -- "a fine, to imprisonment or to both": each of the three consequences is named

§ `Form 5.002 -- Information to obtain a preservation order (subsection 487.013(2)): the 90 days`

-- "The informant therefore requests that (name of the person) be ordered to preserve (specify the computer data) that is in their possession or control when they
-- receive the order for 90 days after the day on which the order is made." The period is kept in the text's own unit (the core's `Length of time`) and as a date test.
-- src:17522 | The informant therefore requests that (name of the person) be ordered to preserve (specify the computer data) that is in their possession or control when they receive the order for 90 days after the day on which the order is made.
@ref Form 5.002 (Subsection 487.013(2)) Information To Obtain a Preservation Order, the period requested (src:17522)
`form 5.002 the period requested` MEANS `Length of time` OF 0, 0, 90, FALSE

-- src:17522 | The informant therefore requests that (name of the person) be ordered to preserve (specify the computer data) that is in their possession or control when they receive the order for 90 days after the day on which the order is made.
@ref Form 5.002 (Subsection 487.013(2)) Information To Obtain a Preservation Order, the period requested (src:17522)
GIVEN `the day on which the order is made` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`form 5.002 the last day of the period requested` MEANS
    `the day on which the order is made` PLUS (`form 5.002 the period requested`)'s days

-- src:17522 | The informant therefore requests that (name of the person) be ordered to preserve (specify the computer data) that is in their possession or control when they receive the order for 90 days after the day on which the order is made.
@ref Form 5.002 (Subsection 487.013(2)) Information To Obtain a Preservation Order, the period requested (src:17522)
GIVEN `the day in question` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the order is made` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`form 5.002 the day is within the period requested` MEANS
    IF `the day in question` GREATER THAN `the day on which the order is made`
       AND `the day in question` AT MOST `form 5.002 the last day of the period requested` `the day on which the order is made`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "for 90 days after the day on which the order is made"

