        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- "If you contravene this order without lawful excuse, you may be subject to a fine, to imprisonment or to both."
-- src:17537 | If you contravene this order without lawful excuse, you may be subject to a fine, to imprisonment or to both.
@ref Form 5.003 (Subsection 487.013(4)) Preservation Order, contravention (src:17537)
GIVEN `the person contravened the order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has a lawful excuse` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`form 5.003 contravening the order without lawful excuse, the person may be subject to a fine, to imprisonment or to both` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the person contravened the order`
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If you contravene this order without lawful excuse"
        IF `the person has a lawful excuse`
        THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "without lawful excuse"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- The destruction duty is the same as in Form 5.001.
-- src:17538 | You are required to destroy the computer data that would not be retained in the ordinary course of business, and any document that is prepared for the purpose of preserving the computer data, in accordance with section 487.0194 of the Criminal Code. If you contravene that provision without lawful excuse, you may be subject to a fine, to imprisonment or to both.
