§ `Form 5.0032 -- Keep account open or active order (subsection 487.0131(3))`

-- "(a) keep the specified account open or active until (insert date) unless the holder of the account requests that you close or deactivate it or this order is revoked or varied;"
-- src:17561 | (a) keep the specified account open or active until (insert date) unless the holder of the account requests that you close or deactivate it or this order is revoked or varied; and
@ref Form 5.0032 (Subsection 487.0131(3)) Keep Account Open or Active Order, paragraph (a) (src:17561)
GIVEN `the day in question` IS A DATE
      `the date inserted in the order` IS A DATE
      `the holder of the account requested that the person close or deactivate it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the order was revoked or varied` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`form 5.0032 para (a) the person is required to keep the specified account open or active` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the day in question` GREATER THAN `the date inserted in the order`
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "until (insert date)"
        IF `the holder of the account requested that the person close or deactivate it`
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless the holder of the account requests that you close or deactivate it"
        IF `the order was revoked or varied`
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "this order is revoked or varied"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- "(b) notify (name of peace officer or public officer) as soon as practicable after the account is closed or deactivated at the request of the holder of the account."
-- Whether the notice was given "as soon as practicable" is an open-textured judgment and is a plain input of the caller, not decided here.
-- src:17562 | (b) notify (name of peace officer or public officer) as soon as practicable after the account is closed or deactivated at the request of the holder of the account.
@ref Form 5.0032 (Subsection 487.0131(3)) Keep Account Open or Active Order, paragraph (b) (src:17562)
GIVEN `the account was closed or deactivated at the request of the holder` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`form 5.0032 para (b) the person is required to notify the peace officer or public officer` MEANS
    IF `the account was closed or deactivated at the request of the holder`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "after the account is closed or deactivated at the request of the holder of the account"

