§ `Form 5.004 -- Information to obtain a production order: which grounds the information states`

-- "The informant says that they have reasonable grounds to suspect (or, if the application is for an order under section 487.014 or 487.0141 of the Criminal Code,
-- reasonable grounds to believe)". The sections the Form is prescribed for are those in its heading; any other section is not covered.
DECLARE `form 5.004 section under which the order is sought` IS ONE OF
    `form 5.004 section 487.014`
    `form 5.004 section 487.0141`
    `form 5.004 section 487.015`
    `form 5.004 section 487.016`
    `form 5.004 section 487.017`
    `form 5.004 section 487.018`
    `form 5.004 another section`

DECLARE `form 5.004 standard of grounds` IS ONE OF
    `form 5.004 reasonable grounds to suspect`
    `form 5.004 reasonable grounds to believe`

-- src:17574 | The informant says that they have reasonable grounds to suspect (or, if the application is for an order under section 487.014 or 487.0141 of the Criminal Code, reasonable grounds to believe)
@ref Form 5.004 (Subsections 487.014(2), 487.0141(2), (5) and (10), 487.015(2), 487.016(2), 487.017(2) and 487.018(3)) Information To Obtain a Production Order, the standard (src:17574)
GIVEN section IS A `form 5.004 section under which the order is sought`
GIVETH A MAYBE `form 5.004 standard of grounds`
`form 5.004 the standard of grounds the information states` MEANS
    CONSIDER section
    WHEN `form 5.004 section 487.014` THEN JUST `form 5.004 reasonable grounds to believe`
    WHEN `form 5.004 section 487.0141` THEN JUST `form 5.004 reasonable grounds to believe`
    WHEN `form 5.004 section 487.015` THEN JUST `form 5.004 reasonable grounds to suspect`
    WHEN `form 5.004 section 487.016` THEN JUST `form 5.004 reasonable grounds to suspect`
    WHEN `form 5.004 section 487.017` THEN JUST `form 5.004 reasonable grounds to suspect`
    WHEN `form 5.004 section 487.018` THEN JUST `form 5.004 reasonable grounds to suspect`
    WHEN `form 5.004 another section` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the Form is prescribed only for the sections its heading names

§ `Form 5.005 -- Production order for documents (subsection 487.014(3))`

-- "The document must be produced to (name of peace officer or public officer) within (time) at (place) in (form)."
-- "(time)" is a number the justice fills in; this encoding counts it in DAYS (assumed, not ruled: NOTES.md F-G). The three conditions are conjoined.
-- src:17614 | The document must be produced to (name of peace officer or public officer) within (time) at (place) in (form).
@ref Form 5.005 (Subsection 487.014(3)) Production Order for Documents, when, where and in what form to produce (src:17614)
GIVEN `the days allowed by the order` IS A NUMBER
      `the days taken to produce the document` IS A NUMBER
      `the document was produced at the place stated in the order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the document was produced in the form stated in the order` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`form 5.005 the document was produced as the order requires` MEANS
    IF `the days taken to produce the document` AT MOST `the days allowed by the order`
       AND `the document was produced at the place stated in the order`
       AND `the document was produced in the form stated in the order`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "within (time) at (place) in (form)"

-- "Therefore, you are ordered to produce a document that is a copy of ... that is in your possession or control when you receive this order (and/or) prepare and
-- produce a document containing ... that is in your possession or control when you receive this order. The document must be produced ... within (time)":
-- the duty as a regulative rule, with the time as an input. The consequence on failure is the one the order states: a fine, imprisonment or both.
-- src:17610 | Therefore, you are ordered to
-- src:17611 | produce a document that is a copy of (specify the document) that is in your possession or control when you receive this order
-- src:17612 | (and/or)
-- src:17613 | prepare and produce a document containing (specify the data) that is in your possession or control when you receive this order.
-- src:17614 | The document must be produced to (name of peace officer or public officer) within (time) at (place) in (form).
@ref Form 5.005 (Subsection 487.014(3)) Production Order for Documents, the order to produce (src:17610-17614)
GIVEN `the days allowed by the order` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `forms 1 to 23 addressee` `forms 5.001 to 5.0091 action`
`form 5.005 the person must produce the document` MEANS
    PARTY `forms 1 to 23 the person to whom the demand, order or summons is addressed`
    MUST `form 5.005 produces the document to the peace officer or public officer`
    WITHIN `the days allowed by the order`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `forms 1 to 23 the person to whom the demand, order or summons is addressed`
         BECAUSE "Form 5.005: the document was not produced within the time stated in the order"

-- src:17617 | If you contravene this order without lawful excuse, you may be subject to a fine, to imprisonment or to both.
@ref Form 5.005 (Subsection 487.014(3)) Production Order for Documents, contravention (src:17617)
GIVEN `the person contravened the order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has a lawful excuse` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`form 5.005 contravening the order without lawful excuse, the person may be subject to a fine, to imprisonment or to both` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the person contravened the order`
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If you contravene this order without lawful excuse"
        IF `the person has a lawful excuse`
        THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "without lawful excuse"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§ `Form 5.0051 -- Production order, specified dates (subsection 487.0141(3))`

-- "(specify up to six dates)": at most six dates may be specified. A count of none is not addressed: the words set a ceiling and no floor.
-- src:17628 | produce a document that is a copy of (specify the document) that is in your possession or control on (specify up to six dates)
-- src:17630 | prepare and produce a document containing (specify the data) that is in your possession or control on (specify up to six dates)
@ref Form 5.0051 (Subsection 487.0141(3)) Production Order -- Specified Dates, the dates specified (src:17628) (src:17630)
GIVEN `the number of dates specified in the order` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`form 5.0051 the number of dates specified is within the limit` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the number of dates specified in the order` GREATER THAN 6
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "specify up to six dates"
        IF `the number of dates specified in the order` AT LEAST 1
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): "up to six" sets a ceiling and says nothing of an order that specifies no date

-- "The document ... must be produced to (name of peace officer or public officer) within (time) of each of the dates specified in this order at (place) in (form)."
-- src:17633 | The document (and if applicable and the copy of the report) must be produced to (name of peace officer or public officer) within (time) of each of the dates specified in this order at (place) in (form).
@ref Form 5.0051 (Subsection 487.0141(3)) Production Order -- Specified Dates, when, where and in what form to produce (src:17633)
GIVEN `the days allowed by the order after the date specified` IS A NUMBER
      `the days taken to produce the document after the date specified` IS A NUMBER
      `the document was produced at the place stated in the order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the document was produced in the form stated in the order` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`form 5.0051 the document was produced as the order requires after a date specified` MEANS
    IF `the days taken to produce the document after the date specified` AT MOST `the days allowed by the order after the date specified`
       AND `the document was produced at the place stated in the order`
       AND `the document was produced in the form stated in the order`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "within (time) of each of the dates specified in this order at (place) in (form)"

-- src:17636 | If you contravene this order without lawful excuse, you may be subject to a fine, to imprisonment or to both.
@ref Form 5.0051 (Subsection 487.0141(3)) Production Order -- Specified Dates, contravention (src:17636)
GIVEN `the person contravened the order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has a lawful excuse` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`form 5.0051 contravening the order without lawful excuse, the person may be subject to a fine, to imprisonment or to both` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the person contravened the order`
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If you contravene this order without lawful excuse"
        IF `the person has a lawful excuse`
        THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "without lawful excuse"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§ `Form 5.006 -- Production order to trace a communication (subsection 487.015(3))`

-- "Therefore, on being served with this order in accordance with subsection 487.015(4) of the Criminal Code, you are ordered to prepare and produce a document containing
-- (specify the transmission data) that is in your possession or control when you are served with this order."
-- "on being served" counts as "where" (the periods ruling): an unserved person is not ordered. Service itself is in subsection 487.015(4), another part.
-- src:17645 | Therefore, on being served with this order in accordance with subsection 487.015(4) of the Criminal Code, you are ordered to prepare and produce a document containing (specify the transmission data) that is in your possession or control when you are served with this order.
@ref Form 5.006 (Subsection 487.015(3)) Production Order To Trace a Communication, the order to produce (src:17645)
GIVEN `the person has been served with the order in accordance with subsection 487.015(4)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the transmission data is in the person's possession or control when the person is served` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`form 5.006 the person is ordered to prepare and produce the document` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the person has been served with the order in accordance with subsection 487.015(4)`
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "on being served with this order in accordance with subsection 487.015(4) of the Criminal Code, you are ordered"
        IF NOT `the transmission data is in the person's possession or control when the person is served`
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "that is in your possession or control when you are served with this order"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- "The document must be produced to (name of peace officer or public officer) as soon as feasible at (place) in (form)."
-- "as soon as feasible" is an open-textured judgment: a plain input of the caller.
-- src:17646 | The document must be produced to (name of peace officer or public officer) as soon as feasible at (place) in (form).
@ref Form 5.006 (Subsection 487.015(3)) Production Order To Trace a Communication, when, where and in what form to produce (src:17646)
GIVEN `the document was produced as soon as feasible` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the document was produced at the place stated in the order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the document was produced in the form stated in the order` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`form 5.006 the document was produced as the order requires` MEANS
    IF `the document was produced as soon as feasible`
       AND `the document was produced at the place stated in the order`
       AND `the document was produced in the form stated in the order`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "as soon as feasible at (place) in (form)"

-- src:17649 | If you contravene this order without lawful excuse, you may be subject to a fine, to imprisonment or to both.
@ref Form 5.006 (Subsection 487.015(3)) Production Order To Trace a Communication, contravention (src:17649)
GIVEN `the person contravened the order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has a lawful excuse` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`form 5.006 contravening the order without lawful excuse, the person may be subject to a fine, to imprisonment or to both` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the person contravened the order`
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If you contravene this order without lawful excuse"
        IF `the person has a lawful excuse`
        THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "without lawful excuse"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

