§ `Forms 5.0032 to 5.0091 -- the right to apply to revoke or vary`

-- "You have the right to apply to revoke or vary this order." (Forms 5.0032, 5.005, 5.0051, 5.006, 5.007, 5.008 and 5.0091 each say it, under "This order is subject to
-- the following conditions"; Form 5.0091 says it after the portions it prohibits.) "You" is the person the order is addressed to; nobody else is named, so another person is not covered.
-- src:17564 | You have the right to apply to revoke or vary this order.
-- src:17616 | You have the right to apply to revoke or vary this order.
-- src:17635 | You have the right to apply to revoke or vary this order.
-- src:17648 | You have the right to apply to revoke or vary this order.
-- src:17665 | You have the right to apply to revoke or vary this order.
-- src:17679 | You have the right to apply to revoke or vary this order.
-- src:17716 | You have the right to apply to revoke or vary this order.
@ref Forms 5.0032 to 5.0091 the right to apply to revoke or vary the order (src:17564) (src:17616) (src:17635) (src:17648) (src:17665) (src:17679) (src:17716)
GIVEN `the person is the person to whom the order is addressed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`forms 5.0032 to 5.0091 the person has the right to apply to revoke or vary the order` MEANS
    IF `the person is the person to whom the order is addressed`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "You have the right to apply to revoke or vary this order"

§ `Form 5.0091 -- Non-disclosure order (subsection 487.0191(3))`

-- "Therefore, you are prohibited from disclosing the existence (or any of the contents or any of the following portion or portions) of the demand (or the order) during a period of
-- (identify the period) after the day on which this order is made." The period is in days (assumed, NOTES.md F-G); it runs from the day after the day of the order, as in Forms 5.002 and 5.0031.
-- src:17714 | Therefore, you are prohibited from disclosing the existence (or any of the contents or any of the following portion or portions) of the demand (or the order) during a period of (identify the period) after the day on which this order is made.
@ref Form 5.0091 (Subsection 487.0191(3)) Non-Disclosure Order, the prohibition (src:17714)
GIVEN `the day in question` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the order is made` IS A DATE
      `the days in the period` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`form 5.0091 the person is prohibited from disclosing on the day` MEANS
    IF `the day in question` GREATER THAN `the day on which the order is made`
       AND `the day in question` AT MOST `the day on which the order is made` PLUS `the days in the period`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "during a period of (identify the period) after the day on which this order is made"

-- The same prohibition as a regulative rule: SHANT with a WITHIN that SUNSETS at the end of the period, which is what "during a period of" says.
-- src:17714 | Therefore, you are prohibited from disclosing the existence (or any of the contents or any of the following portion or portions) of the demand (or the order) during a period of (identify the period) after the day on which this order is made.
@ref Form 5.0091 (Subsection 487.0191(3)) Non-Disclosure Order, the prohibition (src:17714)
GIVEN `the days in the period` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `forms 1 to 23 addressee` `forms 5.001 to 5.0091 action`
`form 5.0091 the person must not disclose` MEANS
    PARTY `forms 1 to 23 the person to whom the demand, order or summons is addressed`
    SHANT `form 5.0091 discloses the existence of the demand or order`
    WITHIN `the days in the period`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `forms 1 to 23 the person to whom the demand, order or summons is addressed`
         BECAUSE "Form 5.0091: the existence of the demand or order was disclosed during the period of the non-disclosure order"

-- src:17717 | If you contravene this order without lawful excuse, you may be subject to a fine, to imprisonment or to both.
@ref Form 5.0091 (Subsection 487.0191(3)) Non-Disclosure Order, contravention (src:17717)
GIVEN `the person contravened the order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has a lawful excuse` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`form 5.0091 contravening the order without lawful excuse, the person may be subject to a fine, to imprisonment or to both` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the person contravened the order`
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If you contravene this order without lawful excuse"
        IF `the person has a lawful excuse`
        THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "without lawful excuse"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE
